# soc-thermal, the zone the fan's trips live in, runs step_wise, not the
# kernel default.
#
# The kernel's default governor here is power_allocator, which steers only a
# zone's last passive trip through cooling devices that have a power model. The
# fan has none, so under it the fan would sit wherever pwm-fan left it -- full
# duty, set at probe. step_wise walks the fan through the zone's active trips,
# and throttles the CPU at its passive one.
#
# The fan's trips are in soc-thermal because Rockchip's thermal driver registers
# one zone per sensor and a fan zone of its own never appears
# (rk3566-microduck-beta.dts says more). So this changes the CPU's governor
# too, and is only for a machine whose DTS puts a fan there: the package is in
# that machine's MACHINE_EXTRA_RRECOMMENDS, never in an image.
#
# Keyed on the zone's type, which is its device-tree node name, never on
# thermal_zoneN: the number follows registration order.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="thermal", KERNEL=="thermal_zone*", ATTR{type}=="soc-thermal", ATTR{policy}="step_wise"
